    "A right triangle has legs of length 9 and 40. What is the length of the hypotenuse?": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 9 squared is 81 and 40 squared is 1600 — add those to get 1681. The square root of 1681 is 41, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has legs of length 11 and 60. What is the length of the hypotenuse?": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 11 squared is 121 and 60 squared is 3600 — add those to get 3721. The square root of 3721 is 61, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has legs of length 28 and 45. What is the length of the hypotenuse?": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 28 squared is 784 and 45 squared is 2025 — add those to get 2809. The square root of 2809 is 53, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has legs of length 33 and 56. What is the length of the hypotenuse?": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 33 squared is 1089 and 56 squared is 3136 — add those to get 4225. The square root of 4225 is 65, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has legs of length 48 and 55. What is the length of the hypotenuse?": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 48 squared is 2304 and 55 squared is 3025 — add those to get 5329. The square root of 5329 is 73, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has legs of length 65 and 72. What is the length of the hypotenuse?": "The Pythagorean theorem says leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. 65 squared is 4225 and 72 squared is 5184 — add those to get 9409. The square root of 9409 is 97, so that's the hypotenuse.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 85 and one leg of 13. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 169, and the hypotenuse squared is 7225. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 7225 minus 169 is 7056. The square root of 7056 is 84, so that's the other leg.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 65 and one leg of 16. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 256, and the hypotenuse squared is 4225. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 4225 minus 256 is 3969. The square root of 3969 is 63, so that's the other leg.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 37 and one leg of 12. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 144, and the hypotenuse squared is 1369. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 1369 minus 144 is 1225. The square root of 1225 is 35, so that's the other leg.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 85 and one leg of 36. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 1296, and the hypotenuse squared is 7225. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 7225 minus 1296 is 5929. The square root of 5929 is 77, so that's the other leg.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 89 and one leg of 39. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 1521, and the hypotenuse squared is 7921. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 7921 minus 1521 is 6400. The square root of 6400 is 80, so that's the other leg.",
    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 101 and one leg of 20. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 400, and the hypotenuse squared is 10201. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 10201 minus 400 is 9801. The square root of 9801 is 99, so that's the other leg.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one angle measures 117°, what does its corresponding angle measure?": "Corresponding angles formed when a transversal crosses parallel lines are always congruent — equal — to each other, so this angle also measures 117 degrees.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one angle measures 73°, what does its alternate interior angle measure?": "Alternate interior angles formed when a transversal crosses parallel lines are always congruent — equal — to each other, so this angle also measures 73 degrees.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one same-side interior angle measures 142°, what does the other same-side interior angle measure?": "Same-side interior angles formed by a transversal crossing parallel lines are supplementary — they add up to 180 degrees. Subtract the one you know from 180: 180 minus 142 is 38 degrees.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one angle measures 88°, what does its vertical angle measure?": "Vertical angles formed when a transversal crosses parallel lines are always congruent — equal — to each other, so this angle also measures 88 degrees.",
    "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. If one angle measures 101°, what does its alternate exterior angle measure?": "Alternate exterior angles formed when a transversal crosses parallel lines are always congruent — equal — to each other, so this angle also measures 101 degrees.",
